              <Comment><![CDATA[<html>
  <head>
    
  </head>
  <body>
    According to Schousboe, rate of invasive cancer is: Rate Invasive = 
    -0.0003717*age + 9.9*(10 -6 )*age 2 - 6.53*(10 -8 )*age 3 + 0.0041328. 
    Relative risks are 1.454 for having family history of breast cancer (and 
    0.938 for not having) and 1.495 for having personal history of breast 
    biopsy (and 0.906 for not having it). As relative risk should be computed 
    as the ratio between the rate of and event in exposed patients and the rate 
    in unexposed patients, we multiply 0.938 and 0.906 to the base rate and 
    then will use 1.454/0.938 and 1.495/0.906 as relative risks, and 
    therefore, their logs as coefficients, that is, 0.4383237 and 0.5008422 
    respectively. Finally, relative risk for breast density was approximated 
    by averaging the relative risks reported in table 3 of the supplement for 
    3 and 4 density levels, Age &lt; 65 years and Age &gt;= years, giving a result 
    of 1.60025 (whose log is 0.4701599)
  </body>
</html>]]></Comment>
